@startuml
' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing the Episodes Act processing flow.
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with minimal partitions,
' one decision point, and explanatory notes instead of nested detail.


title Ghostwriter - Episodes Act Processing

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Parse the act command;
note right
  Expands shorthand, applies the "help" default,
  and separates the act, prompt, and episode selector.
end note

:Load the act definition and configure it;
note right
  Loads built-in or custom TOML, resolves inheritance,
  and applies defaults and prompt values.
end note

:Find project files to process;
note right
  The shared project processor applies module,
  match-rule, and exclusion handling.
end note

if (Specific episodes were requested?) then (yes)
  :Run the selected episodes in request order;
else (no)
  :Run episodes in their defined order;
endif

:Process each selected file through its episode sequence;
note right
  Episodes use the act context and prompt, resolve
  their tools, and call the provider. Repeat and move
  requests control the sequence; an end-task result
  stops further file processing.
end note

:Collect the file result;
note right
  Accumulate results for the caller after processing
  the matching files.
end note

stop

legend right
  * Episodes are ordered steps within one act.
  * A caller can select episodes; otherwise, defined order is used.
  * Episodes can repeat, move, or end task processing.
endlegend
@enduml
